domain AgencyContractCandidate:
  description "Use observed CA-00 boundaries to author an unaccepted first conscious-agency contract."
problem P1:
  |
    The accepted responsibility must become an implementable goal-action-utterance contract
    without treating the existing private goal writer as normative.
premise A1:
  |
    ADR-0027 revision 1 fixes logical ownership. ADR-0025 and ADR-0026 own existing
    Compact V2 separation, partial action acceptance and psyche-only repair. The
    owner authorized commit then plan execution, not new-contract acceptance.
evidence E1:
  |
    CA-00 typed adapter fixtures pass 16 cases. All npm tests and typecheck pass.
    A stored private goal survives actual SQLite save/reload and revision conflict,
    but is absent from Compact V2 conscious input. The provider result uses an empty
    goal and acceptance preserves the prior goal. No paid/network request occurred.
evidence E2:
  |
    Personality and known relationship reach structuredSelf; ability description
    reaches character.basicAction; MP and distance affect allowed candidates.
    The fallback decisionProfile objective remains victory even for enjoyment traits.
    Later action input has no goal or dedicated history, but percepts include
    the just-committed utterance. Ability-only change preserves reaction state.
premise OPTIONS:
  |
    A: Add goal text alone to V2, rejected because writer, initialization and generation
    remain unresolved. B: Separate new frozen generation, reuse existing conscious
    call for initial goal plus action and speech, retain bounded state and old routes.
    C: Add an independent planner and goal store, deferred due extra calls and writers.
pending U1:
  |
    This baseline does not prove model quality or every production branch. Comparative
    model thresholds and budget remain later work. Exact new-contract owner acceptance,
    independent review and any resulting contract ADR are pending.
decision D1 based_on P1, A1, E1, E2, OPTIONS, U1:
  |
    Propose B only as a versioned requirement candidate. One conscious owner creates
    an initial upper goal using explicit author objective when present, otherwise
    personality and known relationship, with victory only a default. Keep author
    prohibitions mandatory. Upper goal is fixed for this first slice; short intent
    changes each decision. Separate intended from committed action/effects.
decision D2 based_on D1, A1, U1:
  |
    Propose new-generation psyche as bounded deterministic reaction with no new
    important-moment trigger; legacy phase routing remains unchanged. Retain existing
    call surfaces, make later redecision share the accepted goal and actual utterance
    facts, and add no new expression repair call. Invalid goal cannot initialize;
    schema-valid speech may survive an invalid action. Failed intent is not persisted
    as an accepted action. Exact bounds and failure combinations belong in the
    candidate for owner review, not runtime implementation.
decision D3 based_on D1, D2, E1, E2, U1:
  |
    Record CA-00 fixtures and rubric, distinguish measured baseline from treatment
    criteria, correct the no-speech overstatement, and complete inventory only for
    that bounded scope. Draft requirement and exact-digest review input under
    requirement-authority-review step 1. Update plan evidence and reviewed Seal
    dependencies. Stop for first owner review; do not independently review or accept
    the candidate, create a contract ADR prematurely, push or use a paid provider.
